  "details": "So, I was in Hubs and the room started lagging out. We were in a teleconference socializer, and for the context of meeting (software developers) it did not really matter if the audio was very clean and concise. There should be an option. Either set by the users, the room designs, or even automatically by the network, that reduces audio quality for the sake of more simultaneous users.\nThis would be a soft block, as opposed to a hard block to having too many users in a room.",
